# G114 — Slide Show

*v2. See `slide-show.md` for prose insights: fluent builder, closed-enum
element shape, per-element durations with optional override, reveal-on-click.*

---

## Choreographic Case: Vault Talk Builder

[talk-builder @title
    IN ORDER TO
        assemble a slide deck from tagged vault notes
        with per-slide reveal choreography

    @talk <- [slide[presentation {title: @title}]]
    @slides <- ![vault[find-by-tag {tag: "talk-slides"}]]

    @talk <- @slides
        where tag has @current-section
        ordered by date ascending
        folded through [slide[add {talk: @talk, slide: @slide-for @note}]]

    -> @talk
]

[talk-present @talk
    IN ORDER TO walk the deck with keyboard-driven reveal

    @cursor <- [slide[cursor {talk: @talk, position: 0, reveal: 0}]]

    until @ended [
        sync @key-events {
            space -> [slide[reveal-next {cursor: @cursor}]]
                     || [slide[advance-slide {cursor: @cursor}]]
            right -> [slide[advance-slide {cursor: @cursor}]]
            left  -> [slide[previous-slide {cursor: @cursor}]]
            home  -> [slide[goto-start    {cursor: @cursor}]]
            end   -> [slide[goto-end      {cursor: @cursor}]]
            q     -> -> @ended
        }

        #current-slide
            slide: @cursor:current-slide
            revealed-up-to: @cursor:reveal
    ]
]

---

## Verb Surface

[slide
    presentation  {title}
    new           {notes?}
    heading       {slide, text, level}         ;; fluent
    bullet        {slide, text, indent}
    image         {slide, path, caption?}
    code          {slide, language, body}
    with-notes    {slide, speaker-notes}
    with-duration {slide, seconds}
    add           {talk, slide}                ;; appends to deck

    cursor        {talk, position, reveal}
    reveal-next   {cursor}                     ;; || if exhausted, fall through to advance
    advance-slide {cursor}
    previous-slide {cursor}
]

---

## Distinctive Innate idiom: fluent chains dissolve

The v1 used method chaining: `slide = slide.heading(...).bullet(...).bullet(...)`.
In Innate, each builder call is a self-contained commission returning the
new slide. Chaining reads as sequence within a block body:

[slide-5
    @s <- [slide[new]]
    @s <- [slide[heading {slide: @s, text: "Results", level: 1}]]
    @s <- [slide[bullet  {slide: @s, text: "40% speedup",    indent: 0}]]
    @s <- [slide[bullet  {slide: @s, text: "no regressions", indent: 0}]]
    @s <- [slide[with-notes {slide: @s,
                              speaker-notes: "emphasize stability"}]]
    -> @s
]

The reassignment pattern `@s <- [...]` is the native equivalent of
the fluent builder. Each step is still a discrete commission.

---

## Demo

[demo
    @talk <- [slide[presentation {title: "My Research"}]]

    @s1 <- [slide[new]]
    @s1 <- [slide[heading {slide: @s1, text: "Motivation", level: 1}]]
    @s1 <- [slide[bullet  {slide: @s1, text: "reveal-on-click", indent: 0}]]
    @s1 <- [slide[bullet  {slide: @s1, text: "pacing budget",   indent: 0}]]

    [slide[add {talk: @talk, slide: @s1}]]

    -> @talk:slide-count        ;; -> 1
    -> @s1:element-count         ;; -> 3
]
